Idempotency helper:

```java
private <T> T idempotent(String commandKey, String operation, String requestHash, Class<T> type, Supplier<T> business, int successStatus)
```

Wait — success status varies: takeover/transfer/action/status return 200, report returns 201 (but report has no commandKey). Replay returns stored status. Controller needs to know status. Let me have service return a small wrapper `CommandResult<T>(int status, T body)`? Or store status in the record and controller always returns 200 for these ops. Simpler: all commandKey ops return 200 (both first and replay). Report returns 201. That's consistent and simple. I'll do that.

Helper logic:

```java
private <T> T runIdempotent(String commandKey, String operation, String hash, Class<T> type, Supplier<T> business) {
    var existing = commandKeys.find(commandKey);
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        return replay(existing.get(), operation, hash, type);
    }
    try {
        commandKeys.insertPlaceholder(commandKey, operation, hash, Instant.now());
    } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
        var committed = commandKeys.findForUpdate(commandKey)
            .orElseThrow(() -> ApiException.conflict("commandKey 冲突"));
        return replay(committed, operation, hash, type);
    }
    T result = business.get();
    commandKeys.fillResponse(commandKey, 200, toJson(result));
    return result;
}

private <T> T replay(CommandKeyRecord rec, String operation, String hash, Class<T> type) {
    if (!rec.operation().equals(operation) || !rec.requestHash().equals(hash)) {
        throw ApiException.conflict("commandKey 已被不同参数使用");
    }
    if (rec.responseBody() == null) {
        throw ApiException.conflict("commandKey 正在处理中");
    }
    return fromJson(rec.responseBody(), type);
